messages:
sara-support: FYI customer upgraded to @redwood/sdk v0.22 and is suddenly hitting 500s from our API. They say certain chat endpoints are missing and the client is emitting duplicate types in payloads. Pasting their minimal repro below.

alex-eng: thanks — can you paste the exact package.json entry + npm/yarn lock? Also which Node version and runtime (serverless/container)?

sara-support: package.json shows "@redwood/sdk": "^0.22.0". Node 18 on a Heroku-like container. Repro steps from customer: npm i @redwood/sdk@0.22 && node example.js. They included this snippet: 

```js
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk';
const c = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
await c.chat.generate({ model: 'redwood-alpha', input: 'hi' });
```

They see a 500: 

```
Error: Unhandled route: POST /v1/chat.generate
    at Router.lookup (/srv/dist/router.js:234:15)
    at processTicksAndRejections (internal/process/task_queues.js:97:5)
```

and server logs show duplicate type defs in request body: `[{type: 'chat'}, {type: 'chat'}]` which trips validation.

alex-eng: hmm. two quick hypotheses: 1) the new client changed how it serializes call targets and some bundlers double-transform ESM->CJS causing duplicate array merges, 2) they pulled an unpublished intermediate package with mismatched API surface. Ask them to run `node -e "console.log(require('@redwood/sdk/package.json').version)"` to confirm the exact installed version. Also ask for a curl repro against our hosted API (no SDK) so we can rule out backend regression.

tim-qa: I pulled the same @0.22 tag in a fresh container and saw `TypeError: body.map is not a function` in the client before hitting the API. Repro below:

```bash
# quick repro
cat > example.js <<'JS'
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/sdk');
const c = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
(async () => {
  try {
    console.log(await c.chat.generate({ model: 'redwood-alpha', input: 'hello' }));
  } catch (e) {
    console.error(e.stack);
  }
})();
JS
node example.js
```

Stack: `TypeError: body.map is not a function` at serializer.js:45. Looks like the client is sometimes passing an object where an array is expected, which then our server-side router treats as a malformed route (hence the Unhandled route error).

alex-eng: thanks tim. can you paste the exact client package.json and dist tree? Might be a build step that inadvertently duplicates type metadata into payload. If the client code emits `{ type: 'chat' }` and our middleware also injects `{ type: 'chat' }` the payload validator could end up with `[obj, obj]` after a shallow-merge.

sara-support: customer ran the `require(...).version` check: returns `0.22.0-alpha.3`. They said they installed `@redwood/sdk@latest` which pulled that alpha. They were unaware.

alex-eng: ah—unpublished alpha got tagged latest accidentally in the mirror. Ops, cc @ops-lincoln. Immediate mitigations: ask customer to pin to 0.21.8, or install exact stable: `npm i @redwood/sdk@0.21.8 --save-exact`. We'll pull the alpha from the registry mirror and set a deprecation tag.

ops-lincoln: I've rolled back the dist tag on the internal mirror and flagged 0.22.0-alpha.3 as deprecated at the registry-level. Also added a temporary server-side acceptance check: if duplicate type entries are detected, we try to dedupe before validation and log the incident. Patch deployed to canary (svr-canary).

ci-bot: Deploy to canary succeeded: build #7821 (ops-lincoln) — all checks green.

tim-qa: verified canary dedupe prevents the 500 and returns a 400 with clearer message now: `InvalidRequest: duplicate message types detected; please upgrade or pin client` — leaving repro tests running.

sara-support: relayed workaround to customer (pin to 0.21.8). They confirmed service restored. They asked if we can proactively alert other customers who pulled latest in the last 48h.

alex-eng: create a mass-scan script to find installations that pulled the alpha via our registry logs and draft a support outbound. I'll also open a small PR to the client repo that validates input types and throws a helpful error client-side before sending.

sara-support: perfect — i'll draft the outbound and add a KB entry: "SDK accidental alpha -> backup pin and repro steps". Closing the thread when outbound is sent. :white_check_mark:
